PartialFillSettler_finaliseAsSettled
├── when fillers[] is empty
│   └── it should revert with InvalidFillers (Pashov A1; previously a no-op — PR #65)
├── when participantCount is zero (no fillers have ever landed)
│   └── it should not transition the order to Refunded via the shared terminal predicate (Pashov A1 early-return)
├── when for a given filler f.premiumSettled is false
│   └── it should skip (continue)
├── when for a given filler f.finalised is already true
│   └── it should skip idempotently
├── when for a given filler f.refunded is true
│   └── it should skip (exclusive paths)
├── for each eligible filler
│   ├── it should set f.finalised to true BEFORE any external call and increment finalisedCount
│   └── it should decrement totalDstCstEscrowed, dstCST.safeTransfer f.dstCstProduced to f.destination, and emit FillerFinalised
├── when the terminal condition holds (hookNonces phase-0 set AND totalDstCstEscrowed == 0 AND finalisedCount == participantCount)
│   └── it should transition orderStatus from Opened to Settled and emit OrderFinalised with status Settled
├── when dstCST.safeTransfer reverts for one filler
│   └── it should credit rescueable[orderDigest][filler] the amount, set f.finalised true, and emit FillerRescueCredited (blacklist-safe — closes #39)
├── when dstCST.safeTransfer reverts for one of three fillers
│   └── it should pay the other two and credit rescueable only for the reverting filler (batch continues)
├── when a reentrant call targets the same fillers[] slice
│   └── it should observe f.finalised true and skip (nonReentrant still guards)
├── when fillers[] contains a duplicate filler address
│   └── it should skip the second occurrence idempotently
├── when a filler slot is eligible for payout
│   └── it should emit OrderAttribution with fillerSlot == premiumFiller == cellarFiller on the happy path (Task 36 / #47)
└── when the payout loop completes
    └── it should assert the settler's dstCST balance >= remaining totalDstCstEscrowed else revert BalanceFloorViolated (Task 37 / #46)
